h__item c-article-authors-search__list-item--left"><a href="/search?author=In%C3%A9s%20Fern%C3%A1ndez%20Maestre" class="c-article-button" data-track="click" data-track-action="author link - publication" data-track-label="link" rel="nofollow">View author publications</a></div><div class="c-article-authors-search__item c-article-authors-search__list-item--right"><p class="search-in-title-js c-article-authors-search__text"><span class="c-article-authors-search__links-text">Search author on:</span><span class="c-article-identifiers"><a class="c-article-identifiers__item" href="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/query.fcgi?cmd=search&amp;term=In%C3%A9s%20Fern%C3%A1ndez%20Maestre" data-track="click" data-track-action="author link - pubmed" data-track-label="link" rel="nofollow">PubMed</a><span class="u-hide"> </span><a class="c-article-identifiers__item" href="https://scholar.google.co.uk/scholar?as_q=&amp;num=10&amp;btnG=Search+Scholar&amp;as_epq=&amp;as_oq=&amp;as_eq=&amp;as_occt=any&amp;as_sauthors=%22In%C3%A9s%20Fern%C3%A1ndez%20Maestre%22&amp;as_publication=&amp;as_ylo=&amp;as_yhi=&amp;as_allsubj=all&amp;hl=en" data-track="click" data-track-action="author link - scholar" data-track-label="link" rel="nofollow">Google Scholar</a></span></p></div></div></li><li id="auth-Sheng_F_-Cai-Aff5"><span class="c-article-authors-search__title u-h3 js-search-name">Sheng F. Cai</span><div class="c-article-authors-search__list"><div class="c-article-authors-search__item c-article-authors-search__list-item--left"><a href="/search?author=Sheng%20F.%20Cai" class="c-article-button" data-track="click" data-track-action="author link - publication" data-track-label="link" rel="nofollow">View author publications</a></div><div class="c-article-authors-search__item c-article-authors-search__list-item--right"><p class="search-in-title-js c-article-authors-search__text"><span class="c-article-authors-search__links-text">Search author on:</span><span class="c-article-identifiers"><a class="c-article-identifiers__item" href="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/query.fcgi?cmd=search&amp;term=Sheng%20F.%20Cai" data-track="click" data-track-action="author link - pubmed" data-track-label="link" rel="nofollow">PubMed</a><span class="u-hide"> </span><a class="c-article-identifiers__item" href="https://scholar.google.co.uk/scholar?as_q=&amp;num=10&amp;btnG=Search+Scholar&amp;as_epq=&amp;as_oq=&amp;as_eq=&amp;as_occt=any&amp;as_sauthors=%22Sheng%20F.%20Cai%22&amp;as_publication=&amp;as_ylo=&amp;as_yhi=&amp;as_allsubj=all&amp;hl=en" data-track="click" data-track-action="author link - scholar" data-track-label="link" rel="nofollow">Google Scholar</a></span></p></div></div></li><li id="auth-Katharina_S_-G_tze-Aff2-Aff6"><span class="c-article-authors-search__title u-h3 js-search-name">Katharina S. Götze</span><div class="c-article-authors-search__list"><div class="c-article-authors-search__item c-article-authors-search__list-item--left"><a href="/search?author=Katharina%20S.%20G%C3%B6tze" class="c-article-button" data-track="click" data-track-action="author link - publication" data-track-label="link" rel="nofollow">View author publications</a></div><div class="c-article-authors-search__item c-article-authors-search__list-item--right"><p class="search-in-title-js c-article-authors-search__text"><span class="c-article-authors-search__links-text">Search author on:</span><span class="c-article-identifiers"><a class="c-article-identifiers__item" href="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/query.fcgi?cmd=search&amp;term=Katharina%20S.%20G%C3%B6tze" data-track="click" data-track-action="author link - pubmed" data-track-label="link" rel="nofollow">PubMed</a><span class="u-hide"> </span><a class="c-article-identifiers__item" href="https://scholar.google.co.uk/scholar?as_q=&amp;num=10&amp;btnG=Search+Scholar&amp;as_epq=&amp;as_oq=&amp;as_eq=&amp;as_occt=any&amp;as_sauthors=%22Katharina%20S.%20G%C3%B6tze%22&amp;as_publication=&amp;as_ylo=&amp;as_yhi=&amp;as_allsubj=all&amp;hl=en" data-track="click" data-track-action="author link - scholar" data-track-label="link" rel="nofollow">Google Scholar</a></span></p></div></div></li><li id="auth-Anastasia_N_-Tikhonova-Aff3-Aff7-Aff8"><span class="c-article-authors-search__title u-h3 js-search-name">Anastasia N. Tikhonova</span><div class="c-article-authors-search__list"><div class="c-article-authors-search__item c-article-authors-search__list-item--left"><a href="/search?author=Anastasia%20N.%20Tikhonova" class="c-article-button" data-track="click" data-track-action="author link - publication" data-track-label="link" rel="nofollow">View author publications</a></div><div class="c-article-authors-search__item c-article-authors-search__list-item--right"><p class="search-in-title-js c-article-authors-search__text"><span class="c-article-authors-search__links-text">Search author on:</span><span class="c-article-identifiers"><a class="c-article-identifiers__item" href="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/query.fcgi?cmd=search&amp;term=Anastasia%20N.%20Tikhonova" data-track="click" data-track-action="author link - pubmed" data-track-label="link" rel="nofollow">PubMed</a><span class="u-hide"> </span><a class="c-article-identifiers__item" href="https://scholar.google.co.uk/scholar?as_q=&amp;num=10&amp;btnG=Search+Scholar&amp;as_epq=&amp;as_oq=&amp;as_eq=&amp;as_occt=any&amp;as_sauthors=%22Anastasia%20N.%20Tikhonova%22&amp;as_publication=&amp;as_ylo=&amp;as_yhi=&amp;as_allsubj=all&amp;hl=en" data-track="click" data-track-action="author link - scholar" data-track-label="link" rel="nofollow">Google Scholar</a></span></p></div></div></li><li id="auth-Ross_L_-Levine-Aff5"><span class="c-article-authors-search__title u-h3 js-search-name">Ross L. Levine</span><div class="c-article-authors-search__list"><div class="c-article-authors-search__item c-article-authors-search__list-item--left"><a href="/search?author=Ross%20L.%20Levine" class="c-article-button" data-track="click" data-track-action="author link - publication" data-track-label="link" rel="nofollow">View author publications</a></div><div class="c-article-authors-search__item c-article-authors-search__list-item--right"><p class="search-in-title-js c-article-authors-search__text"><span class="c-article-authors-search__links-text">Search author on:</span><span class="c-article-identifiers"><a class="c-article-identifiers__item" href="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/query.fcgi?cmd=search&amp;term=Ross%20L.%20Levine" data-track="click" data-track-action="author link - pubmed" data-track-label="link" rel="nofollow">PubMed</a><span class="u-hide"> </span><a class="c-article-identifiers__item" href="https://scholar.google.co.uk/scholar?as_q=&amp;num=10&amp;btnG=Search+Scholar&amp;as_epq=&amp;as_oq=&amp;as_eq=&amp;as_occt=any&amp;as_sauthors=%22Ross%20L.%20Levine%22&amp;as_publication=&amp;as_ylo=&amp;as_yhi=&amp;as_allsubj=all&amp;hl=en" data-track="click" data-track-action="author link - scholar" data-track-label="link" rel="nofollow">Google Scholar</a></span></p></div></div></li><li id="auth-Jennifer_J_-Trowbridge-Aff1"><span class="c-article-authors-search__title u-h3 js-search-name">Jennifer J. Trowbridge</span><div class="c-article-authors-search__list"><div class="c-article-authors-search__item c-article-authors-search__list-item--left"><a href="/search?author=Jennifer%20J.%20Trowbridge" class="c-article-button" data-track="click" data-track-action="author link - publication" data-track-label="link" rel="nofollow">View author publications</a></div><div class="c-article-authors-search__item c-article-authors-search__list-item--right"><p class="search-in-title-js c-article-authors-search__text"><span class="c-article-authors-search__links-text">Search author on:</span><span class="c-article-identifiers"><a class="c-article-identifiers__item" href="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/query.fcgi?cmd=search&amp;term=Jennifer%20J.%20Trowbridge" data-track="click" data-track-action="author link - pubmed" data-track-label="link" rel="nofollow">PubMed</a><span class="u-hide"> </span><a class="c-article-identifiers__item" href="https://scholar.google.co.uk/scholar?as_q=&amp;num=10&amp;btnG=Search+Scholar&amp;as_epq=&amp;as_oq=&amp;as_eq=&amp;as_occt=any&amp;as_sauthors=%22Jennifer%20J.%20Trowbridge%22&amp;as_publication=&amp;as_ylo=&amp;as_yhi=&amp;as_allsubj=all&amp;hl=en" data-track="click" data-track-action="author link - scholar" data-track-label="link" rel="nofollow">Google Scholar</a></span></p></div></div></li></ol></div><h3 class="c-article__sub-heading" id="contributions">Contributions</h3><p>J.J.M. conceptualized the project. J.J.M. and J.J.T. designed experiments. J.J.M., K.A.Y, A.N.F., G.E., A.G.A.-N., P.A.C.D., I.F.M. and S.F.C. performed experiments, and J.J.M., A.N.F., G.E., A.G.A.-N., M.T. and J.J.T. analysed data. J.J.M., A.N.F., G.E., K.S.G., A.N.T., R.L.L. and J.J.T. interpreted data. J.J.M., K.A.Y., M.T. and J.J.T. wrote the manuscript. All authors edited the manuscript.</p><h3 class="c-article__sub-heading" id="corresponding-author">Corresponding author</h3><p id="corresponding-author-list">Correspondence to
                <a id="corresp-c1" aria-label="email Jennifer J. Trowbridge" href="mailto:Jennifer.trowbridge@jax.org">Jennifer J. Trowbridge</a>.</p></div></div></section><section data-title="Ethics declarations"><div class="c-article-section" id="ethics-section"><h2 class="c-article-section__title js-section-title js-c-reading-companion-sections-item" id="ethics">Ethics declarations</h2><div class="c-article-section__content" id="ethics-content">
              
                <h3 class="c-article__sub-heading" id="FPar4">Competing interests</h3>
                <p>S.F.C. is a consultant for Daiichi-Sankyo and Ursamin. He was previously a consultant for Dava Oncology and held equity interest in Imago Biosciences, neither of which are directly related to the content of this paper. R.L.L. is a former member of the Supervisory Board and current SAB member for Qiagen (compensation/equity), a co-founder at Ajax (equity), a board member of the Mark Foundation for Cancer Research and a former scientific advisor to Mission Bio, Kurome, Syndax, Scorpion, Zentalis, Jubilant, Auron, Prelude and C4 Therapeutics; for each of these entitites he received equity/compensation. He has received research support from the Cure Breast Cancer Foundation (with IP rights), Calico, Zentalis and Ajax, and has consulted/provided professional services for ECOG-ACRIN, Genome Canada, Goldman Sachs and Astra Zeneca. J.J.T. has previously received research support from H3 Biomedicine, and patent royalties from Fate Therapeutics. The remaining authors declare no competing interests.</p>
              
            </div></div></section><section data-title="Peer review"><div class="c-article-section" id="peer-review-section"><h2 class="c-article-section__title js-section-title js-c-reading-companion-sections-item" id="peer-review">Peer review</h2><div class="c-article-section__content" id="peer-review-content">
              
              
                <h3 class="c-article__sub-heading" id="FPar3">Peer review information</h3>
                <p><i>Nature Cell Biology</i> thanks Sean Morrison for his contribution to the peer review of this work. <a data-track="click" data-track-label="link" data-track-action="supplementary material anchor" href="/articles/s41556-026-02025-4#MOESM2">Peer reviewer reports</a> are available.</p>
              
            </div></div></section><section data-title="Additional information"><div class="c-article-section" id="additional-information-section"><h2 class="c-article-section__title js-section-title js-c-reading-companion-sections-item" id="additional-information">Additional information</h2><div class="c-article-section__content" id="additional-information-content"><p><b>Publisher’s note</b> Springer Nature remains neutral with regard to jurisdictional claims in published maps and institutional affiliations.</p></div></div></section><section data-title="Extended data"><div class="c-article-section" id="Sec38-section"><h2 class="c-article-section__title js-section-title js-c-reading-companion-sections-item" id="Sec38">Extended data</h2><div class="c-article-section__content" id="Sec38-content"><div data-test="supplementary-info"><div id="figshareContainer" class="c-article-figshare-container" data-test="figshare-container"></div><div class="c-article-supplementary__item js-c-reading-companion-figures-item" data-test="supp-item" id="Fig7"><h3 class="c-article-supplementary__title u-h3"><a data-test="supp-info-link" class="print-link" data-track="call_to_action" data-track-action="view supplementary info" data-track-context="Extended data" data-track-label="extended data fig. 1 additional analysis of single" href="/articles/s41556-026-02025-4/figures/7" data-supp-info-image="//media.springernature.com/lw685/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41556-026-02025-4/MediaObjects/41556_2026_2025_Fig7_ESM.jpg">Extended Data Fig. 1 Additional analysis of single-cell RNA-seq from mice with control or <i>Dnmt3a</i>-mutant hematopoiesis, and SASP versus inflammatory MSC signatures in mouse and human CH.</a></h3><div class="c-article-supplementary__description" data-component="thumbnail-container"><p>(<b>a</b>) Representative PCR genotyping showing wild-type (WT), floxed (fl-R878H) and Cre-recombined (R878H) alleles in <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> Mx-Cre peripheral blood. (<b>b</b>) Frequency of donor (CD45.2<sup>+</sup> tdTomato<sup>+</sup>) hematopoietic cells (left), HSPCs (centre) and HSCs (right) in the BM of recipient mice transplanted with <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> or control Fgd5-CreER hematopoietic cells. P values determined by two-tailed Mann-Whitney test (<i>n</i> = 4 biological replicate recipient mice per condition). (<b>c</b>) Transcript expression of genes defining hematopoietic (<i>Ptprc</i>), MSC (<i>Lepr, Pgfra</i>), Osteoblast (<i>Bgalp2, Col1a1</i>), EC (<i>Pecam1</i>), Arteriolar EC (<i>Cav1</i>) and Sinusoidal EC (<i>Stab2</i>) clusters identified by scRNA-seq. Cells shown are from <i>n</i> = 4 biological replicate recipient mice per condition. (<b>d</b>) Frequency of annotated cell clusters in mice with control or <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> hematopoiesis. Labels are defined in Fig. <a data-track="click" data-track-label="link" data-track-action="figure anchor" href="/articles/s41556-026-02025-4#Fig1">1b</a>. P values determined by two-way ANOVA with uncorrected Fisher’s LSD (<i>n</i> = 4 biological replicate recipient mice per condition). Non-significant p values (P &gt; 0.05) not shown. (<b>e</b>) Normalized enrichment score of DEGs in hematopoietic cell populations in <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> versus control hematopoiesis (<i>n</i> = 4 biological replicate recipient mice per condition). All dots are FDR &lt; 0.05. (<b>f</b>) Frequency of HSPCs with wild-type (+/+) or mutant (R878H/+) <i>Dnmt3a</i> transcripts detectable by scRNA-seq (<i>n</i> = 4 biological replicate recipient mice per condition). Bar graphs show mean +/- SEM. (<b>g</b>) Ranked scatter plot of all GO terms significantly enriched in MSC DEGs from mice with <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> versus control hematopoiesis (<i>n</i> = 4 biological replicate recipient mice per condition). (<b>h</b>) Expression (transcripts per cell) of <i>Cdkn1a, Cdkn2a, Tp53</i> and <i>Mmp14</i> in MSCs from mice with control or <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> hematopoiesis. P values determined by unpaired, two-tailed <i>t</i> test with Welch’s correction of per-cell values (<i>n</i> = 4 biological replicate mice per condition). Non-significant p values (P &gt; 0.05) not shown. (<b>i</b>) Expression of <i>CDKN1A, CDKN2A, TP53</i>, and <i>MMP14</i> in human MSCs from CHIP carriers or non-carriers. P values determined by unpaired, two-tailed <i>t</i> test of per-sample mean values (<i>n</i> = 7 non-carrier individuals, <i>n</i> = 6 CHIP carrier individuals). Non-significant p values (P &gt; 0.05) not shown. (<b>j</b>) Pre-ranked gene set enrichment analysis (GSEA) of DEGs in mice with <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> versus control hematopoiesis. <i>n</i> = 4 biological replicate mice per condition. Normalized enrichment scores (NES) and FDR q-values were calculated using 1,000 gene set permutations in GSEA software. (<b>k</b>) Lollipop plot showing the ranking score for leading edge genes from GSEA in (j). <i>n</i> = 4 biological replicate mice per condition. In box plots, the box represents the interquartile range, the median is indicated by the line inside the box and whiskers extend to the minimum and maximum values. Violin plots show the distribution of single-cell expression values; the line indicates the mean.</p><p><a data-track="click" data-track-label="link" data-track-action="supplementary material anchor" href="/articles/s41556-026-02025-4#MOESM13">Source data</a></p></div></div><div class="c-article-supplementary__item js-c-reading-companion-figures-item" data-test="supp-item" id="Fig8"><h3 class="c-article-supplementary__title u-h3"><a data-test="supp-info-link" class="print-link" data-track="call_to_action" data-track-action="view supplementary info" data-track-context="Extended data" data-track-label="extended data fig. 2 representative flow cytometry" href="/articles/s41556-026-02025-4/figures/8" data-supp-info-image="//media.springernature.com/lw685/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41556-026-02025-4/MediaObjects/41556_2026_2025_Fig8_ESM.jpg">Extended Data Fig. 2 Representative flow cytometry gating and multi-parameter validation of MSC and senescence markers.</a></h3><div class="c-article-supplementary__description" data-component="thumbnail-container"><p>(<b>a</b>) Representative gating of BM hematopoietic cells. (<b>b</b>) Representative gating used to identify and isolate mesenchymal stromal cells (MSCs) and endothelial cells (ECs) <i>in vivo</i> or after co-culture with control or <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> HSPCs. (<b>c</b>) Representative staining of LepR and PDGFRa in whole viable bone marrow. (<b>d</b>) Representative histograms of PDGFRa and LepR staining in ECs and stroma. (<b>e</b>) Representative histograms of LepR staining in PDGFRa<sup>+</sup> and PDGFRa<sup>−</sup> stroma. (<b>f</b>) Representative histograms of PDGFRa staining in LepR<sup>+</sup> and LepR<sup>−</sup> stroma. (<b>g</b>) Representative histograms of SA-b-gal, Bcl-xL and Bcl-2 staining in FMO (fluorescence minus one) control, whole BM, and young and old MSCs. (<b>h</b>) Representative histograms of SA-b-gal staining in FMO control, whole BM, and Bcl-xL<sup>−</sup> Bcl-2<sup>−</sup> MSCs and Bcl-xL<sup>+</sup> Bcl-2<sup>+</sup> MSCs from old mice. (<b>i</b>) Representative staining of Bcl-xL and Bcl-2 in unstained, SA-b-gal<sup>hi</sup> and SA-b-gal<sup>lo</sup> MSCs. (<b>j</b>) Correlation between senescence markers assessed by flow cytometry. Statistical analysis was performed by two-sided Pearson correlation (<i>n</i> = 5 biological replicate mice per condition). P values shown in source data file. (<b>k</b>) Correlation between transcript expression of senescence markers in MSCs with respective MFI of SA-b-gal. Statistical analysis was performed by two-sided Pearson correlation (<i>n</i> = 5 biological replicate mice per condition). P values shown in source data file.</p><p><a data-track="click" data-track-label="link" data-track-action="supplementary material anchor" href="/articles/s41556-026-02025-4#MOESM14">Source data</a></p></div></div><div class="c-article-supplementary__item js-c-reading-companion-figures-item" data-test="supp-item" id="Fig9"><h3 class="c-article-supplementary__title u-h3"><a data-test="supp-info-link" class="print-link" data-track="call_to_action" data-track-action="view supplementary info" data-track-context="Extended data" data-track-label="extended data fig. 3 evaluation of multi-parameter" href="/articles/s41556-026-02025-4/figures/9" data-supp-info-image="//media.springernature.com/lw685/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41556-026-02025-4/MediaObjects/41556_2026_2025_Fig9_ESM.jpg">Extended Data Fig. 3 Evaluation of multi-parameter MSC senescence assessment in positive control mouse models of ageing- and irradiation-induced senescence.</a></h3><div class="c-article-supplementary__description" data-component="thumbnail-container"><p>(<b>a</b>) Experimental design evaluating senescence of MSCs (CD45<sup>−</sup> Ter119<sup>−</sup> CD31<sup>−</sup> CD51<sup>+</sup> PDGFRa<sup>+</sup> LepR<sup>+</sup>) in young (3mo) and old (24mo) wild-type C57BL/6 J mice. (<b>b</b>) Representative histogram (left) and MFI (right) of SA-b-gal in MSCs in young and old mice. P value determined by two-tailed Mann-Whitney test (<i>n</i> = 6 biological replicate mice per condition). (<b>c</b>) Representative Bcl-2 and Bcl-xL staining for young (left) and old (centre) MSCs. Frequency (right) of Bcl-xL<sup>+</sup> Bcl-2<sup>+</sup> MSCs. P value determined by two-tailed Mann-Whitney test (<i>n</i> = 6 biological replicate mice per condition). (<b>d</b>) Representative Bcl-2 and Bcl-xL staining (left) and representative SA-b-gal histogram (centre). Frequency of senescent (SA-b-gal<sup>hi</sup> Bcl-xL<sup>+</sup> Bcl-2<sup>+</sup>) MSCs (right) in young and old mice. P value calculated by two-tailed Mann-Whitney test (<i>n</i> = 6 biological replicate mice per condition). (<b>e</b>) Median FSC (left) and SSC (right) of non-senescent (SA-b-gal<sup>lo</sup> Bcl-xL<sup>−</sup> Bcl-2<sup>−</sup>) and senescent (SA-b-gal<sup>hi</sup> Bcl-xL<sup>+</sup> Bcl-2<sup>+</sup>) MSCs from old mice. P values determined by Mann-Whitney test (<i>n</i> = 6 biological replicate mice per condition). (<b>f</b>) Schematic of experimental design evaluating irradiation-induced senescence of MSCs (CD45<sup>−</sup> Ter119<sup>−</sup> CD31<sup>−</sup> CD51<sup>+</sup> PDGFRa<sup>+</sup> LepR<sup>+</sup>) in p16<sup>INK4A</sup>-3MR mice. (<b>g</b>) Representative histogram (left) and MFI (right) of SA-b-gal in MSCs from control and irradiated p16-3MR mice. P value determined by two-tailed Mann-Whitney test (<i>n</i> = 5 biological replicate mice per condition). (<b>h</b>) Frequency of Bcl-xL<sup>+</sup> Bcl-2<sup>+</sup> MSCs from control and irradiated p16-3MR mice. P value determined by two-tailed Mann-Whitney test (<i>n</i> = 5 biological replicate mice per condition). (<b>i</b>) Frequency of senescent MSCs (SA-b-gal<sup>hi</sup> Bcl-xL<sup>+</sup> Bcl-2<sup>+</sup>) in control and irradiated p16-3MR mice. P value determined by two-tailed Mann-Whitney test (<i>n</i> = 5 biological replicate mice per condition). (<b>j</b>) Representative histogram (left) and MFI (right) of p16 mRFP in MSCs from control and irradiated p16-3MR mice. P value determined by two-tailed Mann-Whitney test (<i>n</i> = 5 biological replicate mice per condition). (<b>k</b>) Representative histogram of p16 mRFP in unstained, SA-b-gal<sup>lo</sup> and SA-b-gal<sup>hi</sup> MSCs. (<b>l</b>) Frequency of senescent MSCs (SA-b-gal<sup>hi</sup> p16-mRFP<sup>hi</sup>) in control and irradiated p16-3MR mice. P value determined by two-tailed Mann-Whitney test (<i>n</i> = 5 biological replicate mice per condition). (<b>m</b>) Median SSC (left) and FSC (right) of non-senescent (SA-b-gal<sup>lo</sup> p16 mRFP<sup>lo</sup>) and senescent (SA-b-gal<sup>hi</sup> p16 mRFP<sup>hi</sup>) MSCs. P value determined by two-tailed Mann-Whitney test (<i>n</i> = 5 biological replicate mice per condition). (<b>n</b>) Median SSC (left) and FSC (right) of non-senescent (SA-b-gal<sup>lo</sup> Bcl-xL<sup>−</sup> Bcl-2<sup>−</sup>) and senescent (SA-b-gal<sup>hi</sup> Bcl-xL<sup>+</sup> Bcl-2<sup>+</sup>) MSCs. P value determined by two-tailed Mann-Whitney test (<i>n</i> = 5 biological replicate mice per condition). Each dot represents an individual biological replicate mouse. For box plots, the box represents the interquartile range, the median is indicated by the line inside the box and whiskers extend to the minimum and maximum values.</p><p><a data-track="click" data-track-label="link" data-track-action="supplementary material anchor" href="/articles/s41556-026-02025-4#MOESM15">Source data</a></p></div></div><div class="c-article-supplementary__item js-c-reading-companion-figures-item" data-test="supp-item" id="Fig10"><h3 class="c-article-supplementary__title u-h3"><a data-test="supp-info-link" class="print-link" data-track="call_to_action" data-track-action="view supplementary info" data-track-context="Extended data" data-track-label="extended data fig. 4 additional experiments interr" href="/articles/s41556-026-02025-4/figures/10" data-supp-info-image="//media.springernature.com/lw685/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41556-026-02025-4/MediaObjects/41556_2026_2025_Fig10_ESM.jpg">Extended Data Fig. 4 Additional experiments interrogating MSC senescence induction by <i>Dnmt3a</i>-mutant hematopoiesis <i>in vivo</i>.</a></h3><div class="c-article-supplementary__description" data-component="thumbnail-container"><p>(<b>a</b>) Schematic of steady state experimental design using <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> Mx-Cre and control Mx-Cre mice. Mice were evaluated &gt; 5 weeks after Mx-Cre induction using poly(I:C). (<b>b</b>) Frequency of Bcl-xL<sup>+</sup> (left) and Bcl-2<sup>+</sup> (right) in MSCs from control and <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> mice. P values calculated by two-tailed Mann-Whitney tests (<i>n</i> = 4 control, <i>n</i> = 5 <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> biological replicate mice). (<b>c</b>) Median SSC (left) and FSC (right) of non-senescent (SA-b-gal<sup>lo</sup> Bcl-xL<sup>−</sup> Bcl-2<sup>−</sup>) and senescent (SA-b-gal<sup>hi</sup> Bcl-xL<sup>+</sup> Bcl-2<sup>+</sup>) MSCs from <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> mice. P values calculated by two-tailed Mann-Whitney tests (<i>n</i> = 4 control, <i>n</i> = 5 <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> biological replicate mice). (<b>d</b>) Correlation between senescence markers in MSCs in control and <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> mice. Significance values determined by two-tailed Pearson correlation (<i>n</i> = 4 control, <i>n</i> = 5 <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> biological replicate mice). P values shown in source data file. (<b>e</b>) Schematic of steady state experimental design using <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> Mx-Cre and control Mx-Cre mice. Mice were evaluated &gt; 5 weeks after Mx-Cre induction using poly(I:C). (<b>f</b>) Frequency of ECs (CD45<sup>−</sup> Ter119<sup>−</sup> CD31<sup>+</sup>) in control and <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> recipient mice. Not significant (P &gt; 0.05) by two-tailed Mann-Whitney test (<i>n</i> = 4 control, <i>n</i> = 5 <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> biological replicate mice). (<b>g</b>) Representative histogram (left) and MFI (right) of SA-b-gal in ECs from control and <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> recipient mice. Not significant (P &gt; 0.05) by two-tailed Mann-Whitney test (<i>n</i> = 4 control, <i>n</i> = 5 <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> biological replicate mice). (<b>h</b>) Frequency of senescent ECs in control and <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> recipient mice. Not significant (P &gt; 0.05) by two-tailed Mann-Whitney test (<i>n</i> = 4 control, <i>n</i> = 5 <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> biological replicate mice). (<b>i</b>) Schematic of steady state experimental design using <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> Fgd5-CreER and control Fgd5-CreER mice. Mice were evaluated &gt; 5 weeks after Fgd5-CreER induction using tamoxifen. (<b>j</b>) Representative histogram (left) and MFI (right) of SA-b-gal in MSCs from control and <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> recipient mice. P value determined by unpaired, two-tailed <i>t</i> test (<i>n</i> = 3 biological replicate mice per condition). (<b>k</b>) Frequency of senescent MSCs in control and <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> recipient mice. P value determined by unpaired, two-tailed <i>t</i> test (<i>n</i> = 3 biological replicate mice per condition). (<b>l</b>) Frequency of Bcl-xL<sup>+</sup> (left) and Bcl-2<sup>+</sup> (right) MSCs in control and <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> recipient mice. P values determined by unpaired, two-tailed <i>t</i> test (<i>n</i> = 3 biological replicate mice per condition). (<b>m</b>) Median SSC (left) and FSC (right) of non-senescent (SA-b-gal<sup>lo</sup> Bcl-xL<sup>−</sup> Bcl-2<sup>−</sup>) and senescent (SA-b-gal<sup>hi</sup> Bcl-xL<sup>+</sup> Bcl-2<sup>+</sup>) MSCs from <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> recipient mice. P values determined by unpaired, two-tailed <i>t</i> test (<i>n</i> = 3 biological replicate mice per condition). (<b>n</b>) Representative histogram (left) and MFI (right) of SA-b-gal in ECs from control and <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> recipient mice. Not significant (P &gt; 0.05) by unpaired, two-tailed <i>t</i> test (<i>n</i> = 3 biological replicate mice per condition). (<b>o</b>) Frequency of senescent ECs in control and <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> recipient mice. Not significant (P &gt; 0.05) by unpaired, two-tailed <i>t</i> test (<i>n</i> = 3 biological replicate mice per condition). (<b>p</b>) Schematic of busulfan-conditioned transplant experimental design using <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> Fgd5-CreER and control Fgd5-CreER donor mice. Transplant was performed &gt; 5 weeks after Fgd5-CreER induction using tamoxifen. (<b>q</b>) Frequency of Bcl-xL<sup>+</sup> (left) and Bcl-2<sup>+</sup> (right) MSCs in control and <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> recipient mice. P value determined by two-tailed Mann-Whitney test (<i>n</i> = 7 biological replicate recipient mice per condition). (<b>r</b>) Median SSC (left) and FSC (right) of non-senescent (SA-b-gal<sup>lo</sup> Bcl-xL<sup>−</sup> Bcl-2<sup>−</sup>) and senescent (SA-b-gal<sup>hi</sup> Bcl-xL<sup>+</sup> Bcl-2<sup>+</sup>) MSCs in and <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> recipient mice. P values determined by Mann-Whitney test (<i>n</i> = 7 biological replicate recipient mice per condition). (<b>s</b>) Schematic of busulfan-conditioned transplant experimental design using <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> Mx-Cre or control Mx-Cre donor mice. Transplant was performed &gt; 5 weeks after poly(I:C) treatment of donor mice. (<b>t</b>) Frequency of Bcl-xL<sup>+</sup> (left) and Bcl-2<sup>+</sup> (right) MSCs in control and <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> recipient mice. P values determined by unpaired, two-tailed <i>t</i> test (<i>n</i> = 10 biological replicate recipient mice per condition). (<b>u</b>) Median SSC (left) and FSC (right) of non-senescent (SA-b-gal<sup>lo</sup> Bcl-xL<sup>−</sup> Bcl-2<sup>−</sup>) and senescent (SA-b-gal<sup>hi</sup> Bcl-xL<sup>+</sup> Bcl-2<sup>+</sup>) MSCs in <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> recipient mice. P values determined by unpaired, two-tailed <i>t</i> test (<i>n</i> = 10 biological replicate recipient mice per condition). (<b>v</b>) Schematic of non-conditioned transplant experimental design using <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> Mx-Cre and control Mx-Cre donor mice. Transplant was performed &gt; 5 weeks after poly(I:C) treatment of donor mice. (<b>w-y</b>) Frequency of donor (CD45.2<sup>+</sup>) cells in the (<b>w</b>) BM, (<b>x</b>) HSPCs, and (<b>y</b>) HSCs of recipient mice at 60 weeks post-transplant. P values determined by unpaired, two-tailed <i>t</i> test with Welch’s correction (<i>n</i> = 8 biological replicate recipient mice per condition). Dots represent individual biological replicate mice. Data in (<b>j-o</b>) include horizontal lines representing mean +/- SEM. In box plots, the box represents the interquartile range, the median is indicated by the line inside the box and whiskers extend to the minimum and maximum values.</p><p><a data-track="click" data-track-label="link" data-track-action="supplementary material anchor" href="/articles/s41556-026-02025-4#MOESM16">Source data</a></p></div></div><div class="c-article-supplementary__item js-c-reading-companion-figures-item" data-test="supp-item" id="Fig11"><h3 class="c-article-supplementary__title u-h3"><a data-test="supp-info-link" class="print-link" data-track="call_to_action" data-track-action="view supplementary info" data-track-context="Extended data" data-track-label="extended data fig. 5 tet2-knockout hematopoiesis i" href="/articles/s41556-026-02025-4/figures/11" data-supp-info-image="//media.springernature.com/lw685/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41556-026-02025-4/MediaObjects/41556_2026_2025_Fig11_ESM.jpg">Extended Data Fig. 5 <i>Tet2</i>-knockout hematopoiesis induces MSC senescence <i>in vivo</i>.</a></h3><div class="c-article-supplementary__description" data-component="thumbnail-container"><p>(<b>a</b>) Schematic of steady state experimental design using <i>Tet2</i><sup>KO</sup> Scl-CreER and control Scl-CreER mice. Mice were evaluated &gt; 5 weeks after Scl-Cre induction using tamoxifen. (<b>b</b>) Representative histogram (left) and MFI (right) of SA-b-gal in MSCs (CD45<sup>−</sup> Ter119<sup>−</sup> CD31<sup>−</sup> CD51<sup>+</sup> PDGFRa<sup>+</sup> LepR<sup>+</sup>) in mice with control or <i>Tet2</i><sup>KO</sup> hematopoiesis. P value determined by unpaired, two-tailed <i>t</i> test (<i>n</i> = 5 biological replicate mice per condition). (<b>c</b>) Frequency of senescent MSCs in mice with control or <i>Tet2</i><sup>KO</sup> hematopoiesis. P value determined by unpaired, two-tailed <i>t</i> test (<i>n</i> = 5 biological replicate mice per condition). (<b>d</b>) Frequency of Bcl-xL<sup>+</sup> (left) and Bcl-2<sup>+</sup> (right) MSCs in mice with control or <i>Tet2</i><sup>KO</sup> hematopoiesis. P values determined by unpaired, two-tailed <i>t</i> test (<i>n</i> = 5 biological replicate mice per condition). (<b>e</b>) Median side scatter (SSC) (left) and forward scatter (FSC) (right) of non-senescent MSCs (SA-b-gal<sup>lo</sup> Bcl-xL<sup>−</sup> Bcl-2<sup>−</sup>) and senescent MSCs (SA-b-gal<sup>hi</sup> Bcl-xL<sup>+</sup> Bcl-2<sup>+</sup>) in <i>Tet2</i><sup><i>KO</i></sup> mice. P values determined unpaired, two-tailed <i>t</i> test (<i>n</i> = 5 biological replicate mice per condition). (<b>f</b>) Representative histogram (left) and MFI (right) of SA-b-gal in ECs (CD45<sup>−</sup> Ter119<sup>−</sup> CD31<sup>+</sup>) in mice with control or <i>Tet2</i><sup>KO</sup> hematopoiesis. Not significant (P &gt; 0.05) by unpaired, two-tailed <i>t</i> test (<i>n</i> = 5 biological replicate mice per condition). (<b>g</b>) Frequency of senescent ECs in mice with control or <i>Tet2</i><sup>KO</sup> hematopoiesis. Not significant (P &gt; 0.05) by unpaired, two-tailed <i>t</i> test (<i>n</i> = 5 biological replicate mice per condition). Dots represent individual biological replicate mice. In box plots, the box represents the interquartile range, the median is indicated by the line inside the box and whiskers extend to the minimum and maximum values.</p><p><a data-track="click" data-track-label="link" data-track-action="supplementary material anchor" href="/articles/s41556-026-02025-4#MOESM17">Source data</a></p></div></div><div class="c-article-supplementary__item js-c-reading-companion-figures-item" data-test="supp-item" id="Fig12"><h3 class="c-article-supplementary__title u-h3"><a data-test="supp-info-link" class="print-link" data-track="call_to_action" data-track-action="view supplementary info" data-track-context="Extended data" data-track-label="extended data fig. 6 additional data on senescence" href="/articles/s41556-026-02025-4/figures/12" data-supp-info-image="//media.springernature.com/lw685/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41556-026-02025-4/MediaObjects/41556_2026_2025_Fig12_ESM.jpg">Extended Data Fig. 6 Additional data on senescence induction in MSCs and its impact on wild-type and <i>Dnmt3a</i>-mutant hematopoiesis.</a></h3><div class="c-article-supplementary__description" data-component="thumbnail-container"><p>(<b>a</b>) Schematic for the co-culture experimental design of control or <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> Mx-Cre HSPCs with wild-type MSCs or BMECs. HSPCs were isolated &gt; 5 weeks after Mx-Cre induction using poly(I:C). (<b>b</b>) Number of adherent CD45<sup>−</sup> MSCs (left) and CD45<sup>+</sup> hematopoietic cells (right) after co-culture. P values determined by unpaired, two-tailed <i>t</i> tests with Welch’s correction (<i>n</i> = 16 biological replicates). Non-significant p values (P &gt; 0.05) not shown. (<b>c</b>) Number of adherent CD45<sup>−</sup> BMECs (left) and CD45<sup>+</sup> hematopoietic cells (right) after co-culture. Non-significant (P &gt; 0.05) by unpaired, two-tailed <i>t</i> tests with Welch’s correction (<i>n</i> = 16 biological replicates). (<b>d</b>) Schematic of transwell experimental design using control or <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> Mx-Cre HSPCs and wild-type MSCs. HSPCs were isolated &gt; 5 weeks after Mx-Cre induction using poly(I:C). (<b>e</b>) Representative histogram (left) and MFI (right) of SA-b-gal in MSCs (CD45<sup>−</sup> CD31<sup>−</sup> CD51<sup>+</sup> PDGFRa<sup>+</sup>) after transwell co-culture with control or <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> HSPCs. P value determined by unpaired, two-tailed <i>t</i> test (<i>n</i> = 7 control, <i>n</i> = 8 <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> biological replicates). (<b>f</b>) Relative expression of <i>Cdkn1a</i> in MSCs after co-culture with control or <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> HSPCs, normalized to <i>Hprt</i> expression. P value determined by unpaired, two-tailed <i>t</i> test with Welch’s correction (<i>n</i> = 12 control, <i>n</i> = 11 <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> biological replicates). (<b>g</b>) Schematic of cell tracer experiment to track replication of MSCs after exposure to CM from control or <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> HSPCs. (<b>h</b>) Frequency of MSCs without cell division after 7-day <i>ex vivo</i> culture with CM from control or <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> HSPCs. P value determined by unpaired, two-tailed <i>t</i> test (<i>n</i> = 6 biological replicates). (<b>i</b>) Heatmap of transcript expression z-scores for genes encoding putative secreted proteins in control and <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> HSCs (<i>n</i> = 4 biological replicate mice). ** symbol denotes proteins detected in HSC/MPP. (<b>j</b>) Schematic of experimental design to determine SASP factors produced from MSCs after treatment with CM from control or <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> HSPCs. (<b>k</b>) Concentration of MMP3 (left), S100a9 (middle) and TNFa (right) produced by MSCs after treatment with control or <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> CM. P values determined by ratio-paired, two-tailed <i>t</i> tests (<i>n</i> = 5 biological replicates per condition). Non<sup>−</sup>significant p values (P &gt; 0.05) not shown. (<b>l</b>) Schematic of experimental design to test the effect of senescent MSCs on wild-type HSPCs <i>ex vivo</i>. (<b>m</b>) Frequency of wild-type HSCs (Lin<sup>−</sup> Sca-1<sup>+</sup> Flt3<sup>−</sup> CD150<sup>+</sup> CD48<sup>−</sup>, left) and GMPs (Lin<sup>−</sup> Sca-1<sup>−</sup> c-Kit<sup>+</sup> CD16/32<sup>+</sup> CD34<sup>+</sup>, right) after 7-day co-culture with non<sup>−</sup>senescent or senescent MSCs. P values determined by unpaired, two-tailed <i>t</i> test (<i>n</i> = 4 biological replicates per condition). (<b>n</b>) Schematic of experimental design to test the effect of senescent MSCs on wild-type hematopoiesis <i>in vivo</i>. (<b>o</b>) Frequency of wild-type (CD45.1<sup>+</sup>) HSCs (Lin<sup>−</sup> Sca-1<sup>+</sup> c-Kit<sup>+</sup> Flt3<sup>−</sup> CD150<sup>+</sup> CD48<sup>−</sup>, left) and GMPs (Lin<sup>−</sup> Sca-1<sup>−</sup> c-Kit<sup>+</sup> CD16/32<sup>+</sup> CD34<sup>+</sup>, right) in mice with control or <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> hematopoiesis. P values determined by unpaired, two-tailed <i>t</i> test with Welch’s correction (<i>n</i> = 8 biological replicates per condition). (<b>p</b>) Schematic of experimental design to test the effect of senescent MSCs on <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> hematopoiesis <i>ex vivo</i>. (<b>q</b>) Frequency of HSCs (Lin<sup>−</sup> Sca-1<sup>+</sup> Flt3<sup>−</sup> CD150<sup>+</sup> CD48<sup>−</sup>, left) and GMPs (Lin<sup>−</sup> Sca-1<sup>−</sup> c-Kit<sup>+</sup> CD16/32<sup>+</sup> CD34<sup>+</sup>, right), after 7-day co-culture of control or <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> HSPCs with wild-type MSCs. P values determined by unpaired, two-tailed <i>t</i> test (<i>n</i> = 17 control, <i>n</i> = 21 <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> biological replicates). Dots represent individual biological replicate mice. In box plots, the box represents the interquartile range, the median is indicated by the line inside the box and whiskers extend to the minimum and maximum values.</p><p><a data-track="click" data-track-label="link" data-track-action="supplementary material anchor" href="/articles/s41556-026-02025-4#MOESM18">Source data</a></p></div></div><div class="c-article-supplementary__item js-c-reading-companion-figures-item" data-test="supp-item" id="Fig13"><h3 class="c-article-supplementary__title u-h3"><a data-test="supp-info-link" class="print-link" data-track="call_to_action" data-track-action="view supplementary info" data-track-context="Extended data" data-track-label="extended data fig. 7 additional data on tnf and il" href="/articles/s41556-026-02025-4/figures/13" data-supp-info-image="//media.springernature.com/lw685/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41556-026-02025-4/MediaObjects/41556_2026_2025_Fig13_ESM.jpg">Extended Data Fig. 7 Additional data on TNF and IL-6 receptor levels and phosphorylation of signalling intermediates in MSCs.</a></h3><div class="c-article-supplementary__description" data-component="thumbnail-container"><p>(<b>a</b>) Schematic of steady state experimental design using control or <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> Mx-Cre mice. Mice were evaluated &gt; 5 weeks after Mx-Cre induction using poly(I:C). (<b>b</b>) Frequency of TNFR1<sup>+</sup> (left), TNFR2<sup>+</sup> (centre), and IL-6R<sup>+</sup> (right) MSCs (CD45<sup>−</sup> Ter119<sup>−</sup> CD31<sup>−</sup> CD51<sup>+</sup> PDGFRa<sup>+</sup> LepR<sup>+</sup>) in control and <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> mice. P values determined by two-tailed Mann-Whitney tests (<i>n</i> = 5 biological replicate mice per condition). Non-significant p values (P &gt; 0.05) not shown. (<b>c</b>) MFI of phospho-proteins pNF-kB (left), pMAPK (centre), and pAKT (right) in MSCs in control and <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> mice. Not significant by two-tailed Mann-Whitney test (<i>n</i> = 5 biological replicate mice per condition). (<b>d</b>) Schematic of busulfan-conditioned recipient mice in transplant experimental design using control or <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> Mx-Cre donor mice. Transplant was performed &gt; 5 weeks after poly(I:C) treatment of donor mice. (<b>e</b>) MFI of phospho-proteins pNF-kB (left), pMAPK (centre), and pAKT (right) in MSCs from mice with control or <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> hematopoiesis. Not significant by two-tailed Mann-Whitney test (<i>n</i> = 10 biological replicate recipient mice per condition). Dots represent individual biological replicate mice. In box plots, the box represents the interquartile range, the median is indicated by the line inside the box and whiskers extend to the minimum and maximum values.</p><p><a data-track="click" data-track-label="link" data-track-action="supplementary material anchor" href="/articles/s41556-026-02025-4#MOESM19">Source data</a></p></div></div><div class="c-article-supplementary__item js-c-reading-companion-figures-item" data-test="supp-item" id="Fig14"><h3 class="c-article-supplementary__title u-h3"><a data-test="supp-info-link" class="print-link" data-track="call_to_action" data-track-action="view supplementary info" data-track-context="Extended data" data-track-label="extended data fig. 8 additional data on p16-3mr co" href="/articles/s41556-026-02025-4/figures/14" data-supp-info-image="//media.springernature.com/lw685/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41556-026-02025-4/MediaObjects/41556_2026_2025_Fig14_ESM.jpg">Extended Data Fig. 8 Additional data on p16-3MR controls and data showing ABT-263 does not directly target <i>Dnmt3a</i>-mutant hematopoietic cells.</a></h3><div class="c-article-supplementary__description" data-component="thumbnail-container"><p>(<b>a</b>) Representative histogram (left) and MFI (right) of p16-mRFP in MSCs (CD45<sup>−</sup> Ter119<sup>−</sup> CD31<sup>−</sup> CD51<sup>+</sup> PDGFRa<sup>+</sup> LepR<sup>+</sup>) in p16-3MR mice with control or <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> hematopoiesis after treatment with vehicle or GCV. P values determined by one-way ANOVA with Tukey’s multiple comparisons test (<i>n</i> = 5 control vehicle, <i>n</i> = 4 control GCV, <i>n</i> = 5 <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> vehicle, <i>n</i> = 7 <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> GCV biological replicate recipient mice). Non-significant p values (P &gt; 0.05) not shown. (<b>b</b>) Frequency of Bcl-xL<sup>+</sup> (left) and Bcl-2<sup>+</sup> (right) MSCs in p16-3MR mice with control or <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> hematopoiesis after treatment with vehicle or GCV. P values determined by one-way ANOVA with Tukey’s multiple comparisons test (<i>n</i> = 5 control vehicle, <i>n</i> = 4 control GCV, <i>n</i> = 5 <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> vehicle, <i>n</i> = 7 <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> GCV biological replicate recipient mice). Non-significant p values (P &gt; 0.05) not shown. (<b>c</b>) Frequency of Bcl-xL<sup>+</sup> (left) and Bcl-2<sup>+</sup> (right) MSCs in recipient mice with control or <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> hematopoiesis treated with vehicle or ABT-263. P values determined by Kruskal-Wallis test with Dunn’s multiple comparisons test (<i>n</i> = 10 control vehicle, <i>n</i> = 10 control ABT-263, <i>n</i> = 9 <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> vehicle, <i>n</i> = 10 <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> ABT-263 biological replicate recipient mice). Non-significant p values (P &gt; 0.05) not shown. (<b>d</b>) Frequency of Bcl-xL<sup>+</sup> (left) and Bcl-2<sup>+</sup> (right) hematopoietic cells in the BM of control Mx-Cre and <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> Mx-Cre mice. Mice were evaluated &gt; 5 weeks after Mx-Cre induction using poly(I:C). Not significant by multiple unpaired, two-tailed <i>t</i> tests (<i>n</i> = 3 biological replicate mice per condition). (<b>e</b>) Schematic of experimental design (left) and number of CFU (right) produced by control and <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> HSPCs treated directly with vehicle or ABT-263 at passage 2 (P2) and passage 3 (P3). P values determined by two-way ANOVA with Tukey’s multiple comparisons test (<i>n</i> = 3 biological replicate mice per condition). (<b>f</b>) Schematic of experimental design evaluating cytokine production from <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> HSPCs following treatment with ABT-263. (<b>g</b>) Concentration of IL-6 (left) or TNFa (right) produced by <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> HSPCs treated with vehicle or ABT-263. Not significant by unpaired, two-tailed <i>t</i> tests (<i>n</i> = 4 biological replicates per condition). (<b>h</b>) Schematic of experimental design evaluating the effects of <i>in vivo</i> ABT-263 administration on wild-type hematopoiesis. (<b>i</b>) Complete blood count values in C57BL/6 J mice treated with vehicle or ABT-263. WBC; white blood cells, NEUT; neutrophils, PLT; platelets. Horizontal dashed lines indicated standard reference values. Not significant by two-tailed Mann-Whitney test (<i>n</i> = 8 biological replicate mice per condition). (<b>j</b>) Frequency of myeloid cells (left) and HSCs (right) in the BM of C57BL/6 J mice treated with vehicle or ABT-263. Not significant by two-tailed Mann-Whitney test (<i>n</i> = 8 biological replicate mice per condition). Dots represent individual biological replicate mice. In box plots, the box represents the interquartile range, the median is indicated by the line inside the box and whiskers extend to the minimum and maximum values.</p><p><a data-track="click" data-track-label="link" data-track-action="supplementary material anchor" href="/articles/s41556-026-02025-4#MOESM20">Source data</a></p></div></div><div class="c-article-supplementary__item js-c-reading-companion-figures-item" data-test="supp-item" id="Fig15"><h3 class="c-article-supplementary__title u-h3"><a data-test="supp-info-link" class="print-link" data-track="call_to_action" data-track-action="view supplementary info" data-track-context="Extended data" data-track-label="extended data fig. 9 in vivo treatment with the se" href="/articles/s41556-026-02025-4/figures/15" data-supp-info-image="//media.springernature.com/lw685/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41556-026-02025-4/MediaObjects/41556_2026_2025_Fig15_ESM.jpg">Extended Data Fig. 9 <i>In vivo</i> treatment with the senolytics dasatinib and quercetin reduce MSC senescence and <i>Dnmt3a-</i>mutant hematopoiesis.</a></h3><div class="c-article-supplementary__description" data-component="thumbnail-container"><p>(<b>a</b>) Schematic of experimental design to generate <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> Mx-Cre hematopoiesis in wild-type recipient mice and treat recipients with dasatinib and quercetin (D + Q). Transplant was performed &gt; 5 weeks after poly(I:C) treatment of donor mice. (<b>b</b>) Representative histogram (left) and MFI of SA-b-gal in MSCs (CD45<sup>−</sup> Ter119<sup>−</sup> CD31<sup>−</sup> CD51<sup>+</sup> PDGFRa<sup>+</sup> LepR<sup>+</sup>) in recipient mice with control or <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> hematopoiesis treated with vehicle or D + Q. P values determined by Brown–Forsythe and Welch ANOVA test with Dunnett’s T3 multiple comparisons test (<i>n</i> = 9 control vehicle, <i>n</i> = 9 control D + Q, <i>n</i> = 8 <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> vehicle, <i>n</i> = 9 <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> D + Q biological replicate recipient mice). Non-significant p values (P &gt; 0.05) not shown. (<b>c</b>) Frequency of senescent MSCs in recipient mice with control or <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> hematopoiesis treated with vehicle or D + Q. P values determined by Brown–Forsythe and Welch ANOVA test with Dunnett’s T3 multiple comparisons test (<i>n</i> = 9 control vehicle, <i>n</i> = 9 control D + Q, <i>n</i> = 8 <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> vehicle, <i>n</i> = 9 <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> D + Q biological replicate recipient mice). Non-significant p values (P &gt; 0.05) not shown. (<b>d</b>) Frequency of Bcl-xL<sup>+</sup> (left) and Bcl-2<sup>+</sup> (right) MSCs in recipient mice with control or <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> hematopoiesis treated with vehicle or D + Q. P values determined by Brown–Forsythe and Welch ANOVA test with Dunnett’s T3 multiple comparisons test (<i>n</i> = 9 control vehicle, <i>n</i> = 9 control D + Q, <i>n</i> = 8 <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> vehicle, <i>n</i> = 9 <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> D + Q biological replicate recipient mice). Non-significant p values (P &gt; 0.05) not shown. (<b>e</b>) Frequency of donor (CD45.2<sup>+</sup>) hematopoietic cells in the BM (left) and HSPC (right) compartment of recipient mice. P values determined by Brown–Forsythe and Welch ANOVA test with Dunnett’s T3 multiple comparisons test (<i>n</i> = 9 control vehicle, <i>n</i> = 9 control D + Q, <i>n</i> = 8 <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> vehicle, <i>n</i> = 9 <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> D + Q biological replicate recipient mice). Non-significant p values (P &gt; 0.05) not shown. (<b>f</b>) Correlation between the frequency of senescent MSCs and donor-derived BM cells (left), and frequency of senescent MSCs and donor-derived HSCs (right) in mice transplanted with control hematopoiesis. Significance values determined by two-tailed Pearson correlation (<i>n</i> = 9 biological replicate mice per condition). (<b>g</b>) Correlation between the frequency of senescent MSCs and donor-derived BM cells (left), and frequency of senescent MSCs and donor-derived HSCs (right) in mice transplanted with <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> hematopoiesis. Significance values determined by two-tailed Pearson correlation (<i>n</i> = 8 <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> vehicle, <i>n</i> = 9 <i>Dnmt3a</i><sup>R878H/+</sup> D + Q biological replicate mice). Dots represent individual biological replicate mice. In box plots, the box represents the interquartile range, the median is indicated by the line inside the box and whiskers extend to the minimum and maximum values.</p><p><a data-track="click" data-track-label="link" data-track-action="supplementary material anchor" href="/articles/s41556-026-02025-4#MOESM21">Source data</a></p></div></div><div class="c-article-supplementary__item js-c-reading-companion-figures-item" data-test="supp-item" id="Fig16"><h3 class="c-article-supplementary__title u-h3"><a data-test="supp-info-link" class="print-link" data-track="call_to_action" data-track-action="view supplementary info" data-track-context="Extended data" data-track-label="extended data fig. 10 msc senescence in other gene" href="/articles/s41556-026-02025-4/figures/16" data-supp-info-image="//media.springernature.com/lw685/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41556-026-02025-4/MediaObjects/41556_2026_2025_Fig16_ESM.jpg">Extended Data Fig. 10 MSC senescence in other genetic mouse models of human AML.</a></h3><div class="c-article-supplementary__description" data-component="thumbnail-container"><p>(<b>a</b>) Schematic of experimental design to evaluate induction of MSC senescence by <i>Npm1;Flt3</i><sup>ITD</sup> and <i>Idh1;Npm1;Nras</i><sup>G12D</sup> AML in busulfan-conditioned wild-type recipient mice. (<b>b</b>) Complete blood count values in mice transplanted with AML or control BM. MONO; monocytes, PLT; platelets. P values determined by Brown–Forsythe and Welch ANOVA with Dunnett’s T3 multiple comparisons test (<i>n</i> = 4 biological replicate mice per condition). Non-significant p values (P &gt; 0.05) not shown. (<b>c</b>) Frequency of senescent MSCs (CD45<sup>−</sup> Ter119<sup>−</sup> CD31<sup>−</sup> CD51<sup>+</sup> PDGFRa<sup>+</sup> LepR<sup>+</sup>) in recipient mice transplanted with AML or control BM. P values determined by Brown–Forsythe and Welch ANOVA with Dunnett’s T3 multiple comparisons test (<i>n</i> = 4 biological replicate mice per condition). Non-significant p values (P &gt; 0.05) not shown. (<b>d</b>) Schematic of experimental design to evaluate induction of MSC senescence by <i>Npm1;Flt3</i><sup>ITD</sup> and <i>Idh1;Npm1;Nras</i><sup>G12D</sup> AML in irradiated wild-type recipient mice. (<b>e</b>) Complete blood count values in mice with transplanted with AML or control BM. MONO; monocytes, PLT; platelets. P values determined by Brown–Forsythe and Welch ANOVA with Dunnett’s T3 multiple comparisons test (<i>n</i> = 5 control, <i>n</i> = 5 <i>Npm1;Flt3</i><sup>ITD</sup> AML, <i>n</i> = 4 <i>Idh1;Npm1;Nras</i><sup>G12D</sup> AML biological replicate mice per condition). Non-significant p values (P &gt; 0.05) not shown. (<b>f</b>) Frequency of senescent MSCs in recipient mice transplanted with AML or control BM. P values determined by Brown–Forsythe and Welch ANOVA with Dunnett’s T3 multiple comparisons test (<i>n</i> = 5 control, <i>n</i> = 5 <i>Npm1;Flt3</i><sup>ITD</sup> AML, <i>n</i> = 4 <i>Idh1;Npm1;Nras</i><sup>G12D</sup> AML biological replicate mice per condition). Non-significant p values (P &gt; 0.05) not shown. (<b>g</b>) Expression of <i>CDKN1A</i> in human MSCs from aged-matched normal BM, non-<i>DNMT3A</i>/<i>TET2-</i>mutant AML, and <i>DNMT3A</i>- or <i>TET2-</i>mutant AML. Data from Chen et al. P values determined by Kruskal-Wallis with uncorrected Dunn’s test (<i>n</i> = 8 normal BM, <i>n</i> = 33 non-<i>DNMT3A</i>/<i>TET2-</i>mutant AML, <i>n</i> = 29 <i>DNMT3A</i>- or <i>TET2-</i>mutant AML). Dots represent individual biological replicate mice or human samples. In box plots, the box represents the interquartile range, the median is indicated by the line inside the box and whiskers extend to the minimum and maximum values.</p><p><a data-track="click" data-track-label="link" data-track-action="supplementary material anchor" href="/articles/s41556-026-02025-4#MOESM22">Source data</a></p></div></div></div></div></div></section><section data-title="Supplementary information"><div class="c-article-section" id="Sec39-section"><h2 class="c-article-section__title js-section-title js-c-reading-companion-sections-item" id="Sec39">Supplementary information</h2><div class="c-article-section__content" id="Sec39-content"><div data-test="supplementary-info"><div class="c-article-supplementary__item" data-test="supp-item" id="MOESM1"><h3 class="c-article-supplementary__title u-h3"><a data-test="supp-info-link" class="print-link" data-track="call_to_action" data-track-action="view supplementary info" data-track-context="Supplementary information" data-track-label="reporting summary" href="https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41556-026-02025-4/MediaObjects/41556_2026_2025_MOESM1_ESM.pdf" data-supp-info-image="">Reporting Summary (download PDF <svg width="16" height="16" focusable="false" role="img" aria-hidden="true" class="u-icon"><use xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="#icon-eds-i-download-medium"></use></svg>)</a></h3></div><div class="c-article-supplementary__item" data-test="supp-item" id="MOESM2"><h3 class="c-article-supplementary__title u-h3"><a data-test="supp-info-link" class="print-link" data-track="call_t